   "evidence": "Basic.lean:828 uses `reidemeisterTorsion_of_not_finite` for the field-level torsion. The new file has no `_of_not_finite` counterpart: grep finds no `not_finite` in Componentwise.lean.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Algebra/Homology/ReidemeisterTorsion/Componentwise.lean",
   "fix": "Add `componentwiseReidemeisterTorsion_of_not_finite (hn : \u00ac{i | n i \u2260 0}.Finite) : C.componentwiseReidemeisterTorsion c f = 0`, proved via `eq_componentwiseReidemeisterTorsion_iff` and `reidemeisterTorsion_of_not_finite`. It should probably be `@[simp]`, like the base-field version if that one is.",
   "issue": "The `componentwiseReidemeisterTorsion` docstring says a component is `0` 'when `C` is unbounded'. No lemma states this, and every zero/unit lemma (`mk_componentwiseReidemeisterTorsion_eq_zero_iff`, `isUnit_componentwiseReidemeisterTorsion_iff`, `componentwiseReidemeisterTorsion_eq_zero_iff`) requires `hn : {i | n i \u2260 0}.Finite`. The unbounded case therefore has no usable statement.",
   "line": 203
  }
 ],
